WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.542
Meet Northstar Industrial, a growing industrial technology company.

00:00:03.542 --> 00:00:12.840
Maya Tan, the CEO, wants higher sales, lower operating cost, and faster execution—but without creating another disconnected collection of AI tools.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:16.383
Northstar uses Flolah as a single operating layer.

00:00:16.383 --> 00:00:22.139
Company context, objectives, agents, workflows, business systems, policies, budgets, and channels stay connected.

00:00:22.139 --> 00:00:24.795
This is Maya's normal user view.

00:00:24.795 --> 00:00:35.422
She can see the operating pulse of the company immediately, while the shared Knowledge area gives every authorised agent the same governed business context.

00:00:35.422 --> 00:00:40.479
Northstar's organisation is designed as one team of people and AI workers.

00:00:40.479 --> 00:00:43.429
Maya and her operations lead remain accountable.

00:00:43.429 --> 00:00:49.328
Specialist agents cover sales development, revenue operations, customer success, procurement, finance, and operating coordination.

00:00:49.328 --> 00:00:55.228
Each agent has a clear role, an owner, permitted tools, and an explicit budget.

00:00:55.228 --> 00:01:02.392
This avoids the common AI journey where separate teams buy separate assistants, duplicate work, and lose accountability.

00:01:02.392 --> 00:01:09.555
In Flolah, delegation follows the organisation, and the CEO can see who—or what—is responsible for each outcome.

00:01:09.555 --> 00:01:14.179
Northstar's yearly direction is translated into quarterly objectives and measurable key results.

00:01:14.179 --> 00:01:21.886
The leadership team can see targets for qualified pipeline, conversion, customer retention, procurement savings, and operating efficiency in one place.

00:01:21.886 --> 00:01:26.124
Objectives are not presentation slides that disappear after a review meeting.

00:01:26.124 --> 00:01:31.519
Goals and work are linked back to the measure they are expected to move.

00:01:31.519 --> 00:01:37.684
Progress can be updated from business events, CRM and ERP records, workflow results, and agent reports.

00:01:37.684 --> 00:01:44.234
When a measure drifts, the company can respond while there is still time to change the outcome.

00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.386
Objectives become action through explicit goals.

00:01:46.386 --> 00:01:52.481
Northstar's active goals are linked to quarterly initiatives and assigned to the agent accountable for the result.

00:01:52.481 --> 00:01:55.708
The sales team follows up qualified pipeline on weekdays.

00:01:55.708 --> 00:01:57.500
Collections works the receivables cycle.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:02.520
Inventory watches replenishment and the operating team reviews the OKR control tower every week.

00:02:02.520 --> 00:02:10.049
Each goal has a cadence, an end date aligned to the objective period, and a clear prompt describing the expected evidence.

00:02:10.049 --> 00:02:17.578
This is the bridge between a measure on a dashboard and autonomous work that happens without Maya repeatedly asking for it.

00:02:17.578 --> 00:02:20.094
Objectives become repeatable execution through workflows.

00:02:20.094 --> 00:02:28.061
Northstar has flows for lead qualification, opportunity follow-up, customer risk, procurement review, invoice follow-up, and the executive operating rhythm.

00:02:28.061 --> 00:02:36.447
A workflow is more than a scheduled automation: it gives agents a governed sequence of events, decisions, actions, and evidence.

00:02:36.447 --> 00:02:41.478
The same process can run consistently every day, while exceptions are visible.

00:02:41.478 --> 00:02:50.284
Teams can improve the workflow once and let every future run benefit, instead of relying on tribal knowledge or one-off prompts.

00:02:50.284 --> 00:02:56.680
For sales growth, Northstar keeps governed CRM activity in the customer and opportunity system of record.

00:02:56.680 --> 00:03:03.475
This is the live CRM module, opened directly on Northstar's synthetic opportunity list—not a copied reporting table.

00:03:03.475 --> 00:03:08.672
The company label and SSO permission keep Maya inside the Northstar tenant boundary.

00:03:08.672 --> 00:03:15.068
Sales agents can prioritise follow-up, prepare account context, and report pipeline movement against the quarterly objective.

00:03:15.068 --> 00:03:25.462
Maya can move from the objective to the underlying commercial activity and see whether the company is building enough qualified pipeline to reach the revenue target.

00:03:25.462 --> 00:03:31.528
Northstar's ERP connects suppliers, items, invoices, and operational records to the same company context.

00:03:31.528 --> 00:03:39.761
This is the live Sales Invoice list, opened directly inside the Northstar company rather than the generic ERP home.

00:03:39.761 --> 00:03:49.293
Procurement and finance agents can monitor supplier decisions, cost-saving opportunities, and invoice follow-up while preserving ERP as the transactional source of truth.

00:03:49.293 --> 00:04:00.559
This is how Northstar reduces cost without losing control: agents analyse and coordinate the work, workflows standardise it, and the business system retains the authoritative record.

00:04:00.559 --> 00:04:06.816
Northstar is configured for end-to-end autonomous operation where the company has decided autonomy is appropriate.

00:04:06.816 --> 00:04:12.239
Read, internal-write, and approved external communication actions can proceed without routine human approval.

00:04:12.239 --> 00:04:15.159
High-impact financial or destructive actions remain prohibited.

00:04:15.159 --> 00:04:19.748
These rules are centrally visible and apply across agents and workflows.

00:04:19.748 --> 00:04:22.668
Autonomy therefore does not mean removing control.

00:04:22.668 --> 00:04:31.012
It means deciding the control model once, making it explicit, and allowing routine work to move quickly inside those boundaries.

00:04:31.012 --> 00:04:33.734
AI work must also be economically accountable.

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:39.179
Northstar assigns token and operating budgets by agent, then measures usage, errors, and efficiency.

00:04:39.179 --> 00:04:47.736
The company can invest more in agents that move important key results and investigate agents that consume resources without producing enough value.

00:04:47.736 --> 00:04:50.458
This connects AI cost to operating outcomes.

00:04:50.458 --> 00:04:59.015
Instead of discovering an uncontrolled bill at month end, Maya has a live view of the capacity allocated across her digital workforce.

00:04:59.015 --> 00:05:03.409
Maya does not need to visit every screen to run the company.

00:05:03.409 --> 00:05:10.365
Flolah can channel requests, exceptions, summaries, and progress updates through the COO agent and connected channels such as WhatsApp.

00:05:10.365 --> 00:05:19.152
A request can be routed to the right agent, executed through the right workflow, checked against policy and budget, and reported back with evidence.

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:29.770
The UI remains available for inspection and control, while the day-to-day executive experience is simple: ask, review the outcome, and intervene only when the system surfaces a real exception.

00:05:29.770 --> 00:05:38.981
Without this operating layer, Northstar's AI journey would fragment across chat tools, spreadsheets, CRM automations, ERP scripts, and personal assistants.

00:05:38.981 --> 00:05:45.429
Context would drift, ownership would blur, and every integration would become a new island.

00:05:45.429 --> 00:05:56.483
With Flolah, objectives provide direction; agents provide specialised capacity; workflows provide repeatability; CRM and ERP provide business truth; and policies and budgets provide control.

00:05:56.483 --> 00:06:07.537
The result is a company that can pursue sales growth, cost reduction, and operating efficiency as one coordinated system—and improve that system every quarter.
